00:00:05.772 --> 00:00:08.908
just filed in the $1.6 billion.

00:00:09.042 --> 00:00:11.144
The Dominion Voting Systems

00:00:11.144 --> 00:00:13.113
lawsuit against Fox News.

00:00:13.113 --> 00:00:13.446
Right now,

00:00:13.446 --> 00:00:14.447
I want to bring in our senior

00:00:14.447 --> 00:00:16.249
media reporter, Oliver Darcy.

00:00:16.249 --> 00:00:16.950
CNN legal

00:00:16.950 --> 00:00:17.584
analyst Norm

00:00:17.584 --> 00:00:20.420
Eisen and CNN media analyst Sara Fischer.

00:00:20.587 --> 00:00:22.622
Oliver, so what is revealed in these

00:00:22.622 --> 00:00:24.190
new filings?

00:00:24.190 --> 00:00:24.758
That's right, Wolf.

00:00:24.758 --> 00:00:26.559
These are really astonishing new details

00:00:26.559 --> 00:00:27.527
that we're getting

00:00:27.527 --> 00:00:28.261
first glimpse

00:00:28.261 --> 00:00:30.063
at as part of a new legal filing

00:00:30.063 --> 00:00:32.332
that was just made public moments ago.

00:00:32.432 --> 00:00:34.334
And in it, Rupert Murdoch,

00:00:34.334 --> 00:00:36.036
he acknowledges

00:00:36.036 --> 00:00:37.470
that some of his top hosts

00:00:37.470 --> 00:00:38.371
over at Fox

00:00:38.371 --> 00:00:41.374
News were peddling false election claims.

00:00:41.408 --> 00:00:42.142
This comes

00:00:42.142 --> 00:00:44.244
in a deposition that we're first

00:00:44.244 --> 00:00:45.078
we're seeing

00:00:45.078 --> 00:00:46.813
as a result of this new legal filing.

00:00:46.813 --> 00:00:48.148
And I want to read to you

00:00:48.148 --> 00:00:49.916
part of it, Wolf.

00:00:49.916 --> 00:00:50.517
In it,

00:00:50.517 --> 00:00:52.652
Rupert Murdoch is asked by Dominion.

00:00:52.652 --> 00:00:53.820
You were aware now

00:00:53.820 --> 00:00:55.255
that Fox did more than simply

00:00:55.255 --> 00:00:56.222
host these guests

00:00:56.222 --> 00:00:58.558
and give them a platform. Correct. And

00:00:59.559 --> 00:01:00.960
Murdoch goes on and it says,

00:01:00.960 --> 00:01:01.528
in fact,

00:01:01.528 --> 00:01:02.662
you are now aware

00:01:02.662 --> 00:01:04.330
that Fox endorsed at times

00:01:04.330 --> 00:01:06.433
this false notion of a stolen election.

00:01:06.699 --> 00:01:08.701
Murdoch says not Fox, not Fox,

00:01:08.701 --> 00:01:10.470
but maybe Lou Dobbs,

00:01:10.470 --> 00:01:13.606
maybe Maria Bartiromo as commentators.

00:01:14.007 --> 00:01:15.175
And then it goes on.

00:01:15.175 --> 00:01:15.842
And he meant

00:01:15.842 --> 00:01:17.243
they mentioned Jeanine Pirro,

00:01:17.243 --> 00:01:18.478
a Fox News host.

00:01:18.478 --> 00:01:20.580
He says, I think she did as well.

00:01:20.580 --> 00:01:22.849
Yeah. Lou Dobbs. Oh, a lot.

00:01:23.183 --> 00:01:25.285
Fox host Sean Hannity a bit.

00:01:25.552 --> 00:01:27.253
And then it goes on to say

00:01:27.253 --> 00:01:28.188
as well

00:01:28.188 --> 00:01:28.922
about Fox

00:01:28.922 --> 00:01:30.123
endorsing the narrative

00:01:30.123 --> 00:01:32.025
of a stolen election. Correct.

00:01:32.025 --> 00:01:33.393
Rupert Murdoch answers

00:01:33.393 --> 00:01:34.727
know some of our commentators

00:01:34.727 --> 00:01:36.262
were endorsing it

00:01:36.262 --> 00:01:37.797
and the media says

00:01:37.797 --> 00:01:38.798
about their endorsement

00:01:38.798 --> 00:01:40.533
of a stolen election.

00:01:40.533 --> 00:01:42.902
Rupert Murdoch says, yes, they endorsed.

00:01:43.636 --> 00:01:45.672
This also comes as the deposition

00:01:45.872 --> 00:01:47.841
reveals, again, the disdain

00:01:47.841 --> 00:01:48.608
that Rupert Murdoch

00:01:48.608 --> 00:01:50.043
had for these election lies.

00:01:50.043 --> 00:01:51.377
He referred to them at once,

00:01:51.377 --> 00:01:53.413
one point as B.S.

00:01:53.580 --> 00:01:55.582
and damaging in an email.

00:01:55.615 --> 00:01:57.684
And he's also said that he wishes

00:01:57.684 --> 00:01:58.785
the network

00:01:58.785 --> 00:02:00.186
did more to tamp down

00:02:00.186 --> 00:02:01.754
these conspiracy theories.

00:02:01.754 --> 00:02:04.057
Of course, hindsight, Wolf, is 20, 20.

00:02:04.057 --> 00:02:04.958
And when you're being sued

00:02:04.958 --> 00:02:06.626
for $1.6 billion,

00:02:06.626 --> 00:02:07.627
that might

00:02:07.894 --> 00:02:08.828
result in you

00:02:08.828 --> 00:02:10.296
wishing you did things a different way.

00:02:10.296 --> 00:02:11.097
Absolutely.

00:02:11.097 --> 00:02:11.531
And Norm,

00:02:11.531 --> 00:02:13.199
what else stands out to you

00:02:13.199 --> 00:02:14.534
in this brand new brief

00:02:14.534 --> 00:02:15.702
that has just been released?

00:02:15.702 --> 00:02:17.170
And just how serious

00:02:17.170 --> 00:02:19.472
is the legal threat right now

00:02:19.472 --> 00:02:21.941
that is available for Fox?

00:02:21.941 --> 00:02:22.342
Wolf,

00:02:22.342 --> 00:02:23.977
I think it's quite serious

00:02:23.977 --> 00:02:27.180
because when you go beyond

00:02:27.180 --> 00:02:29.282
reporting, Fox defense,

00:02:29.282 --> 00:02:30.550
well, we were just reporting.

00:02:30.550 --> 00:02:32.318
But when you go beyond reporting

00:02:32.318 --> 00:02:33.720
and your chairman admits

00:02:33.720 --> 00:02:35.522
there was endorsement,

00:02:35.522 --> 00:02:37.891
then that opens you up to liability

00:02:37.891 --> 00:02:39.993
under the actual malice standard.

00:02:39.993 --> 00:02:43.263
And, Wolf, it's not just $1.6 million.

00:02:43.263 --> 00:02:46.332
If the jury decides that this conduct

00:02:46.332 --> 00:02:47.600
was egregious enough

00:02:47.600 --> 00:02:50.670
and much that is in here continues to be

00:02:50.670 --> 00:02:52.472
shocking, that's bristling

00:02:52.472 --> 00:02:53.907
almost 200 pages.

00:02:53.907 --> 00:02:56.109
Every page has a Perry Mason moment.

00:02:56.476 --> 00:02:59.212
If the jury decides that it was bad

00:02:59.212 --> 00:03:02.882
enough conduct, they can double or triple

00:03:03.183 --> 00:03:06.452
that $1.6 billion or go even higher.

00:03:06.619 --> 00:03:08.788
So I think there's very serious

00:03:08.788 --> 00:03:09.689
legal exposure.

00:03:09.689 --> 00:03:11.224
This is one of the most

00:03:11.224 --> 00:03:13.426
devastating depositions

00:03:13.426 --> 00:03:14.561
that I've ever seen.

00:03:14.561 --> 00:03:15.495
That's a ton of money,

00:03:15.495 --> 00:03:17.931
too, potentially at stake for Foxborough.

00:03:17.931 --> 00:03:19.365
As Oliver just reported,

00:03:19.365 --> 00:03:21.367
some of Fox's biggest stars

00:03:21.601 --> 00:03:23.403
are named in this deposition.

00:03:23.403 --> 00:03:24.737
Maria Bartiromo,

00:03:24.737 --> 00:03:26.372
Jeanine Pirro, Lou Dobbs,

00:03:26.372 --> 00:03:27.607
formerly with Fox.

00:03:27.607 --> 00:03:29.342
Sean Hannity still with Fox.

00:03:29.342 --> 00:03:30.610
What kind of an impact

00:03:30.610 --> 00:03:32.378
is this having on the network?

00:03:34.247 --> 00:03:35.648
It's having a huge impact, Wolf,

00:03:35.648 --> 00:03:37.350
because it's a major distraction.

00:03:37.350 --> 00:03:37.617
I mean,

00:03:37.617 --> 00:03:38.618
this network is going to have

00:03:38.618 --> 00:03:40.687
to cover the 2024 election

00:03:40.687 --> 00:03:41.754
in which Donald Trump

00:03:41.754 --> 00:03:42.989
is going to participate.

00:03:42.989 --> 00:03:45.091
He is still spewing election lies

00:03:45.091 --> 00:03:46.960
on his own truth social platform.

00:03:46.960 --> 00:03:47.827
And so every time

00:03:47.827 --> 00:03:48.861
they're going to have to revisit

00:03:48.861 --> 00:03:50.964
election coverage, this will haunt them.

00:03:50.964 --> 00:03:52.832
But I think a big finding from today,

00:03:52.832 --> 00:03:54.000
Wolf, is that, yes,

00:03:54.000 --> 00:03:55.635
we know that these hosts knew

00:03:55.635 --> 00:03:56.703
that this was bad.

00:03:56.703 --> 00:03:57.604
That deposition

00:03:57.604 --> 00:03:58.705
from last month

00:03:58.705 --> 00:04:00.740
saw exchanges of text messages

00:04:00.740 --> 00:04:01.541
in which the Tucker

00:04:01.541 --> 00:04:02.976
Carlson of the world conceded

00:04:02.976 --> 00:04:04.110
this was a problem.

00:04:04.110 --> 00:04:05.411
But what's new today

00:04:05.411 --> 00:04:07.547
is that the top level executives

00:04:07.547 --> 00:04:09.349
also knew in real time

00:04:09.349 --> 00:04:10.083
this was bad

00:04:10.083 --> 00:04:11.718
and they did nothing to stop it.

00:04:11.718 --> 00:04:12.385
In fact,

00:04:12.385 --> 00:04:13.052
Fox's

00:04:13.052 --> 00:04:14.220
chief legal

00:04:14.220 --> 00:04:15.655
and policy officer

00:04:15.655 --> 00:04:17.223
is quoted in the deposition

00:04:17.223 --> 00:04:18.658
basically saying that Fox

00:04:18.658 --> 00:04:20.226
had a responsibility

00:04:20.226 --> 00:04:21.661
to stop these election lies

00:04:21.661 --> 00:04:22.562
from being peddled

00:04:22.562 --> 00:04:24.931
and it's still acted anyway.

00:04:24.931 --> 00:04:26.499
So, Oliver, button this up for us.

00:04:26.499 --> 00:04:28.601
Where does this lawsuit go from here?

00:04:29.335 --> 00:04:29.836
This lawsuit

00:04:29.836 --> 00:04:31.604
looks like it's going to trial, Wolf,

00:04:31.604 --> 00:04:34.107
next month. It's supposed to start.

00:04:34.140 --> 00:04:35.575
And, you know, Fox,

00:04:35.575 --> 00:04:36.309
I should note,

00:04:36.309 --> 00:04:38.411
too, is pushing back against what

00:04:38.411 --> 00:04:39.612
we're reading right now.

00:04:39.612 --> 00:04:40.413
And they're saying that

00:04:40.413 --> 00:04:41.381
Dominion effectively

00:04:41.381 --> 00:04:42.882
has a very weak case.

00:04:42.882 --> 00:04:43.683
But legal experts

00:04:43.683 --> 00:04:45.051
I've spoken to

00:04:45.051 --> 00:04:46.386
have have suggested

00:04:46.386 --> 00:04:47.320
complete otherwise

00:04:47.320 --> 00:04:48.788
and that they have said

00:04:48.788 --> 00:04:49.555
that this evidence

00:04:49.555 --> 00:04:50.857
that we're seeing presented now

00:04:50.857 --> 00:04:53.026
for the first time in these filings

00:04:53.026 --> 00:04:54.360
is really quite damning.

00:04:54.360 --> 00:04:55.528
Well, let me ask Durham,

00:04:55.528 --> 00:04:58.064
is there a strong legal case here?

00:04:58.064 --> 00:05:00.333
Wolf, I do think it is a powerful

00:05:00.333 --> 00:05:01.067
legal case.

00:05:01.067 --> 00:05:03.169
The standard of actual malice

00:05:03.169 --> 00:05:06.472
that you need to prove that Fox either

00:05:06.639 --> 00:05:08.041
knew these were lies

00:05:08.041 --> 00:05:09.842
or recklessly disregarded.

00:05:09.842 --> 00:05:13.112
The truth is very high in our country.

00:05:13.112 --> 00:05:14.647
The First Amendment protects

00:05:14.647 --> 00:05:16.749
the freedom of the press abroad.

00:05:16.749 --> 00:05:18.484
An array of conversations.

00:05:18.484 --> 00:05:19.686
But here you have

00:05:19.686 --> 00:05:21.688
the damning admissions,

00:05:21.688 --> 00:05:24.357
including from the top guy, Rupert

00:05:24.357 --> 00:05:26.092
Murdoch himself, that he knew

00:05:26.092 --> 00:05:27.727
these things were not so.

00:05:27.727 --> 00:05:30.897
And that Fox, he admits they endorsed.

00:05:31.230 --> 00:05:34.834
I think Fox is facing very serious legal

00:05:34.834 --> 00:05:35.501
exposure.

00:05:35.501 --> 00:05:36.602
And Tucker

00:05:36.602 --> 00:05:37.904
Carlson comes in

00:05:37.904 --> 00:05:38.838
for damaging

00:05:38.838 --> 00:05:40.973
reporting in this brief as well.

00:05:40.973 --> 00:05:41.841
Sarah, how do you see

00:05:41.841 --> 00:05:42.742
this thing playing out

00:05:44.644 --> 00:05:46.713
I think they go to trial in April

00:05:46.713 --> 00:05:47.980
and then I think after that,

00:05:47.980 --> 00:05:51.084
if it is found that Fox loses this case,

00:05:51.084 --> 00:05:51.884
your coverage is going

00:05:51.884 --> 00:05:52.752
to be much different

00:05:52.752 --> 00:05:54.120
for the next election, Wolf.

00:05:54.120 --> 00:05:55.321
If Fox doesn't get

00:05:55.321 --> 00:05:56.856
you know, Fox gets away with this.

00:05:56.856 --> 00:05:58.791
What's to stop them from pushing

00:05:58.791 --> 00:06:00.126
further narratives in the future

00:06:00.126 --> 00:06:01.227
that are completely false

00:06:01.227 --> 00:06:03.296
and not just them other media companies?

00:06:03.296 --> 00:06:06.065
This case sets a huge precedent

00:06:06.065 --> 00:06:07.100
for freedom of the press,

00:06:07.100 --> 00:06:08.067
but also for how

00:06:08.067 --> 00:06:09.635
we policed misinformation

00:06:09.635 --> 00:06:11.437
moving forward for elections to come.

00:06:11.437 --> 00:06:12.004
You know, the stakes

00:06:12.004 --> 00:06:13.539
clearly are enormous right now.

00:06:13.539 --> 00:06:14.374
Sarah Fisher,

00:06:14.374 --> 00:06:16.576
Oliver Darcy, Norm Eisen, guys, thank you

00:06:16.576 --> 00:06:17.477
